        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T04:15:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "iiuc the vendor command will also use flash_log_dequeue_event() using the same log_read_context.\ncan we also have a non-destructive log-peek function, which can be called from the console w/o affecting what the vendor command can get next time. I envision the vendor command can be called periodically to retrieve log entries so that they can be included in feedback reports or analyzed in UMA.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 303,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 303,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ebc48ef88e03bf7d61cc37edb5cb667be97f2bc0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79740d41_0f228348",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 303,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T14:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking about letting the user keep the context, but thought it was an overkill: so what if sometimes reading the log will require scanning it - this will not take much time and will happen very infrequently, I am not sure extra complexity is needed\n\nMaybe leave it as future enhancement?",
      "parentUuid": "8d3c2b4a_578a9f37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 303,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 303,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ebc48ef88e03bf7d61cc37edb5cb667be97f2bc0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da1c70d2_4421321c",
        "filename": "common/flash_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 429,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-21T04:15:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "don\u0027t we need to also reset log_write_cursor, so that the next flash_log_add_event() starts writing from the beginning?\nand don\u0027t we want to reset log_read_context so that it starts returning no entries after erasing? basically, clear the cached version when we erase the flash.\nand if so, erasing may need to go after the flash_log_dequeue_event() loop.",
      "revId": "ebc48ef88e03bf7d61cc37edb5cb667be97f2bc0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
